4.3.1.10 InitBufPool
Function Usage
Initializes the TBufPool buffer resource pool. This API applies to the scenario
where you want to manually specify UB/L1 buffer resource reuse when buffer
resources are limited. After initialization, a child resource pool is allocated from
the overall buffer resources. The child resource pool TBufPool provides the
following resource management modes:
● The reloading API of TPipe::InitBufPool is reused with other TBufPool child
resource pools.
● TBufPool:: 4.3.3.3 InitBufPool continues to divide child resource pools.
● TBufPool:: 4.3.3.4 InitBuffer allocates buffers.
For details about the TBufPool and resource allocation diagram, see 4.3.3
TBufPool.
